# =====================================================================
# Hangug Deulama — Frontend Environment Configuration
# =====================================================================
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (next to package.json) and set the variables
# that match the environment you are running the app in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# All variables MUST be prefixed with `VITE_` to be exposed to the
# client-side bundle by Vite. Restart `npm run dev` after editing.
#
# The frontend works in TWO modes:
#
#   1. LOCAL  — backend served by XAMPP / Laragon / MAMP at
#               http://localhost/hangug-api/public
#               Used for academic demos / mentor walkthrough.
#
#   2. PRODUCTION — backend served at
#               https://api.appriyo.com/hangug
#               Used for the deployed demo.
#
# Pick ONE of the two VITE_API_BASE_URL presets below and comment out
# the other, or write your own. Leave it BLANK for same-origin
# deployments where the API is mounted at `/api/...` on the same host.
# =====================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTION 1 — LOCAL development (XAMPP)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Use this when you are running the PHP API on your own machine via
# XAMPP / Laragon / MAMP and want to demo the project to your mentor.
#
#   1. Start Apache + MySQL from the XAMPP control panel.
#   2. Place the PHP backend in:  C:\xampp\htdocs\hangug-api\
#      so it is reachable at:    http://localhost/hangug-api/public
#   3. Import docs/DATABASE_DESIGN.md schema into MySQL.
#   4. Uncomment ONLY the local line below.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost/hangug-api/public


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTION 2 — PRODUCTION (shared hosting)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Use this when the project is being shown from the deployed demo.
# The full backend runs at api.appriyo.com and is mounted under
# the `/hangug` path. The Axios client automatically appends `/api`
# to this base URL.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.appriyo.com/hangug
